  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 808.01 Required Health Effects Language for Regulated Synthetic Organics Chemical (SOC) Contaminants and Per- and Polyfluoroalkyl Substances (PFAS) Contaminants",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 808.01 Required Health Effects Language for Regulated Synthetic Organics Chemical (SOC) Contaminants and Per- and Polyfluoroalkyl Substances (PFAS) Contaminants. The O/O shall use the statements specified in this part, as applicable, as the statement required by Env-Dw 801.03(a)(3) to describe the adverse health effects for the synthetic organic chemical (SOC) contaminants specified in Env-Dw 705.02 and the per- and polyfluoroalkyl substances (PFAS) contaminants specified in Env-Dw 705.06.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Dw 800) #9730, eff 6-30-10; ss by #12675, eff 1-1-19; ss by #12838, eff 9-30-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw800.html"
